          "content": {
            "size": 1795,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "[{\"id\":\"633bf627-ae12-4aba-b597-92b0ececdc1f\",\"title\":\"increase in flu\",\"description\":\"Between December 21st, 2025 and December 28th, 2025, a total of 458 communicable disease cases were reported in All Regions. The overall trend has decreased by 10.9% compared to the previous period. The most prevalent illness was the Flu, particularly in the delhi district if 'All Regions' is selected\",\"priority\":\"Medium\",\"target_district_id\":null,\"status\":\"Active\",\"issued_by\":null,\"issued_date\":\"2025-12-28\",\"created_at\":\"2025-12-28T07:13:49.335742+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-12-28T07:13:49.335742+00:00\",\"district_id\":\"6ca13619-8b37-456e-a3cd-6794ac83ff70\"}, \n {\"id\":\"7fefdcf2-391d-4671-826f-f6bdbb0d32b1\",\"title\":\"Malaria outbreak\",\"description\":\"\\nFor the outbreak of malaria, kindly follow these :\\n1. Use insect repellent on exposed skin. The most effective repellents are EPA-registered and contain 20-35% DEET or 20% picaridin.\\n2. Wear protective clothing such as loose-fitting, light-colored, long-sleeved shirts and long pants. Tucking pants into socks or boots provides extra protection.\\n3. Sleep under an insecticide-treated bed net (ITN) if your room is not air-conditioned or well-screened. These nets act as both a physical and chemical barrier and are widely used in endemic areas.\\n4. Stay in well-screened or air-conditioned rooms and ensure all windows and doors are kept closed.\\n5. Spray an insecticide or repellent in your bedroom before going to bed.\\nAvoid outdoor activity during peak mosquito biting hours (dusk to dawn). \",\"priority\":\"High\",\"target_district_id\":null,\"status\":\"Active\",\"issued_by\":null,\"issued_date\":\"2025-12-28\",\"created_at\":\"2025-12-28T05:05:33.14088+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-12-28T05:05:33.14088+00:00\",\"district_id\":\"3e5cfd54-8b06-4093-906b-148afd099a93\"}]"
